Ben: I really want to study French. I think it sounds beautiful.
Amy: Why French? Do you want to go to France one day?
Ben: Yes, and French is used by many international organisations.
Amy: That''s true. I''d like to learn Russian myself.
Ben: Russian? Why is that?
Amy: My father does business with Russians, so I can help him.
Ben: That''s a great reason. Good luck with it!', 'Amy 问 Ben 想学哪门外语;Ben 想学法语,觉得好听;因为想去法国、且许多国际组织用法语;Amy 想学俄语;因为父亲和俄罗斯人做生意,她可以帮忙。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Which language does Ben want to study?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["French.","Russian.","German.","Japanese."]},{"q":"Why does Ben like that language?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["It is the easiest to spell.","He thinks it sounds beautiful.","It has the most speakers.","His teacher chose it."]},{"q":"Which language does Amy want to learn?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Russian.","French.","Arabic.","Korean."]},{"q":"Why does Amy want to learn it?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["To watch cartoons.","Her father does business with Russians.","To travel to France.","Because it is required at school."]},{"q":"What is one extra reason Ben gives for his choice?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["It is spoken only in France.","No one else speaks it.","Many international organisations use it.","It has no grammar."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'required1', 'U5');
Chinese and English have the most native speakers.
The official languages of the United Nations are spoken by billions of people.
People study a foreign language for many different reasons.
Learning one opens a door to a new way of thinking.', '当今世界约有七千种语言;汉语和英语母语者最多;联合国官方语言被数十亿人使用;人们学外语原因各异;学一门语言会打开通往新思维方式的大门。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"About how many languages are there in the world?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["About seventy.","About seven million.","Only two.","About seven thousand."]},{"q":"Which two languages have the most native speakers?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Chinese and English.","French and German.","Russian and Arabic.","Korean and Japanese."]},{"q":"Who speaks the UN''s official languages?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Only a few people.","Billions of people.","Nobody today.","Only students."]},{"q":"Why do people study a foreign language?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["For only one reason.","Because they are forced to.","For many different reasons.","To forget their own language."]},{"q":"What does learning a language open, according to the passage?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["A shop.","A window to the past only.","A box of money.","A door to a new way of thinking."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'required1', 'U5');
Martin: Pants? That''s funny. I don''t usually shop for pants with friends.
Zhou Wei: You don''t? Don''t you want someone to tell you if they look good?
Martin: Wait, do you mean trousers, the ones we wear on our legs?
Zhou Wei: Yes! That''s American English for trousers.
Martin: Ah, I see. In British English, ''pants'' means underwear.
Zhou Wei: Oh! No wonder you looked surprised.
Martin: Don''t worry. It''s just two ways of speaking the same language.', '周伟说要买 pants;Martin 觉得好笑;原来周伟说的是美式英语里的''裤子'';而英式英语里 pants 指内裤;两人弄懂这只是同一语言的两种说法。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What did Zhou Wei want to buy?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Trousers (he called them ''pants'').","A pair of shoes.","A new book.","Some food."]},{"q":"Why did Martin find it funny at first?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["He had no money.","He thought ''pants'' meant underwear.","He did not like Zhou Wei.","He could not hear well."]},{"q":"In American English, what does ''pants'' mean?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Underwear.","Shoes.","Trousers.","A hat."]},{"q":"In British English, what does ''pants'' mean?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Trousers.","A coat.","Socks.","Underwear."]},{"q":"How does Martin explain the difference?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["It is two ways of speaking the same language.","One of them is wrong.","Zhou Wei made a mistake.","English is too hard."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'required1', 'U5');
Ancient people carved symbols onto animal bones and shells.
By the Shang Dynasty, these became a complete writing system.
No matter what dialect people speak, they can read the same characters.
In this way, written Chinese has helped to unite the people.', '汉字数千年前始于简单的图画;古人把符号刻在动物骨头和龟甲上;到商朝已成完整书写系统;不论说什么方言,人们都能读同样的字;这样汉字帮助团结了人民。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What did written Chinese begin as?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Spoken sounds only.","Simple pictures.","Foreign words.","Modern letters."]},{"q":"Where did ancient people carve the symbols?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["On paper books.","On metal coins.","On animal bones and shells.","On glass."]},{"q":"By which dynasty had it become a complete system?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["The Tang Dynasty.","The Ming Dynasty.","No dynasty.","The Shang Dynasty."]},{"q":"Who can read the same characters?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["People who speak different dialects.","Only one region.","Only scholars.","Only foreigners."]},{"q":"What has written Chinese helped to do?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Divide the people.","Unite the people.","End all dialects.","Replace speaking."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'required1', 'U5');
Jia Xin: Try listening to English radio every day.
Wang Le: Does that really help?
Jia Xin: Yes. It helps you get used to how fast native speakers talk.
Wang Le: That''s a good idea. What else can I do?
Jia Xin: Record your own voice and compare it with the speaker''s.
Wang Le: I see. So I can hear my own mistakes.
Jia Xin: Exactly. Little by little, your listening will improve.', '王乐听力困难求建议;佳欣建议每天听英语广播;能帮助习惯母语者语速;还建议录下自己声音和原声比较,听出自己的错误;一点点听力就会进步。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What problem does Wang Le have?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Trouble with writing.","Trouble with reading.","Trouble with listening.","Trouble with spelling."]},{"q":"What is Jia Xin''s first piece of advice?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Stop studying English.","Only read silently.","Watch films with no sound.","Listen to English radio every day."]},{"q":"How does that advice help?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["It helps you get used to native speakers'' speed.","It saves money.","It makes English easier to spell.","It teaches new grammar rules."]},{"q":"What is the second piece of advice?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Speak only Chinese.","Record your voice and compare it.","Never listen to others.","Read the dictionary."]},{"q":"What will happen little by little?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Wang Le will give up.","His English will get worse.","His listening will improve.","Nothing will change."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'required1', 'U5');
Do not be afraid to make mistakes when you speak.
Every mistake is a chance to learn something new.
If you are not sure what a word means, just ask politely.
A few brave words today can open many doors tomorrow.', '给学新语言的人一个小贴士:说话时别怕犯错;每个错误都是学新东西的机会;不确定词义就礼貌地问;今天几句勇敢的话,明天能打开许多扇门。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Who is this tip for?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Only teachers.","Only children.","Only native speakers.","Anyone learning a new language."]},{"q":"What does the speaker say about making mistakes?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Do not be afraid of them.","Never speak at all.","Mistakes are useless.","Avoid speaking to anyone."]},{"q":"What is every mistake, according to the passage?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["A reason to quit.","A chance to learn something new.","A waste of time.","A serious problem."]},{"q":"What should you do if unsure of a word''s meaning?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Pretend to understand.","Stop the conversation.","Just ask politely.","Speak only Chinese."]},{"q":"What can a few brave words today do?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Cost a lot of money.","Make people angry.","Waste your time.","Open many doors tomorrow."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'required1', 'U5');

